% n22: the eliminator's BRANCH types are checked. Same declarations as p15, but the
% `true` branch is fed `f : P false` where `P true` is demanded. If the builder put
% the branches in the wrong order, or the codomain substitution were wrong, this
% would slip through. It must be 24 (argument type mismatch) on both arms.
1 sort 0
2 const Bool
3 const Bool
inductive Bool : 1 | true : 2 | false : 3
elim Bool_cases Bool 0
4 const Bool
5 sort 0
6 pi 4 5
axiom P : 6
7 const P
8 const true
9 app 7 8
axiom t : 9
10 const P
11 const false
12 app 10 11
axiom f : 12
13 const Bool_cases
14 const P
15 app 13 14
16 const f
17 app 15 16
18 const P
19 const false
20 app 18 19
check 17 : 20
